The `config_manager_init` function initializes the configuration manager with the given sources and fallback data. It uses dynamic memory allocation for efficient resource utilization. The function also includes a fallback mechanism in case certain configuration values are missing or corrupted.

Additional functionality, such as seamless integration of new data sources, handling large-scale deployments without compromising performance, and balancing high availability with efficient resource utilization can be added by extending the existing functions or implementing new ones.

