The random number generator is implemented within a namespace and class structure, including a constructor and destructor for the class. A static member variable is used to store the random number generator instance. The code does not include data processing functions or mechanisms for load balancing, caching, or integration with existing network management systems as per your request. Those components would require significant additional development based on specific requirements and constraints.']

['```java
import java.io.*;
import java.net.URL;
import java.security.MessageDigest;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.logging.Level;
import java.util.logging.Logger;

public final class TextProcessor {
    private static final Logger LOGGER = Logger.getLogger(TextProcessor.class.getName());
    private static final int MAX_HASH_LENGTH = 1000;
    private List<String> dataSources;

    public TextProcessor(List<String> dataSources) {
        this.dataSources = dataSources;
    }

    public void process() throws IOException {
        for (String dataSource : dataSources) {
            try (BufferedReader reader = getReader(dataSource)) {
                String line;
                StringBuilder text = new StringBuilder();
                while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                    if (!line.trim().isEmpty()) {
                        text.append(line);
                    }
                }
                byte[] hash = computeMD5Hash(text.toString());
                String hexHash = bytesToHex(hash);
                System.out.println(hexHash.substring(0, Math.min(hexHash.length(), MAX_HASH_LENGTH)));
            } catch (Exception e) {
                LOGGER.log(Level.WARNING, "Error processing data source: " + dataSource, e);
            }
        }
    }

    private BufferedReader getReader(String dataSource) throws IOException {
        if (dataSource.startsWith("http")) {
            return new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(new URL(dataSource).openStream()));
        } else {
            return new BufferedReader(new FileReader(dataSource));
        }
    }

    private byte[] computeMD5Hash(String input) {
        try {
            MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5");
            md.update(input.getBytes());
            return md.digest();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            throw new RuntimeException(e);
        }
    }

    private String bytesToHex(byte[] hash) {
        StringBuilder hexString = new StringBuilder();
        for (byte b : hash) {
            hexString.append(String.format("%02x", b));
        }
        return hexString.toString();
    }
}
```

To use the TextProcessor, create a list of data sources (file paths or URLs), and pass it to the constructor:

