The maximum number of messages that can be stored is dynamically set with the `set_max_messages()` function, triggering a log warning when the limit is reached. A callback function is provided to notify the application when a message is removed due to exceeding the maximum limit.

A statistics collection feature tracks the total number of messages added, removed, and the average duration of message retrieval operations. The statistics are periodically reported to an external monitoring system via the `report_statistics()` function, ensuring that the reporting process does not interfere with real-time message handling.']

