This code creates a pool of worker threads that process incoming data packets from a queue. The queue is implemented using an array with dynamic resizing to handle high-throughput scenarios. Memory management is handled with malloc, realloc and free functions. Thread safety is ensured using pthread_mutex_lock and pthread_mutex_unlock for the queue operations and semaphores for signaling when the queue is not empty.

The worker threads continuously process packets until a termination signal is received. This design allows for dynamic scaling based on current load and efficient handling of peak traffic without compromising performance. To ensure graceful shutdown, worker threads are joined before exiting the main function.

