The provided code also includes support for periodic updates of the array contents, log printing for debugging and monitoring performance under stress conditions, optimizations for multi-threaded environments, and a mechanism to validate and clean up resources when the array is no longer needed. The implementation uses pthreads for synchronization between multiple threads concurrently accessing and modifying the array, providing thread safety and efficient locking mechanisms.

The `init_and_update_array` function initializes the first structure with a seed value and starts updating the remaining structures in parallel using multiple threads created by calling `pthread_create`. The error handling is minimal as it only checks for memory allocation failures and initialization failures in the `initialize_structure` function. Developers can further extend this code to handle potential delays or data inconsistencies during updates gracefully.']

