The code uses a read-write lock (rwlock) for thread safety when managing the array in a multi-threaded application. The `pthread_rwlock_wrlock` function is used to obtain a write lock, while `pthread_rwlock_unlock` is used to release it. This allows multiple threads to read from the array concurrently without conflicts but ensures that only one thread can modify it at a time.

The code also includes two example functions for logging information (logInfo) and updating the array with new data (updateEntry). These are run in separate threads using pthreads. The logInfo function uses printf to output the current state of the array, while the updateEntry function modifies an element of the array and updates its timestamp accordingly.

Finally, startLoggingAndUpdating is a convenience function that creates logging and updating threads for the given RxUnitArray object.']

