The implementation searches for the first occurrence of `str1` in the forward list and performs the necessary operations as described in the task requirements. The chosen design handles edge cases such as an empty list or when `str1` does not exist in the list.

To reduce node reallocations, the helper function `batchUpdate()` is used to group consecutive elements of the same value before performing the actual insertions based on the `insertBefore` flag. This reduces the number of node reallocations and improves performance under the given constraint target.

It's important to note that this implementation maintains the integrity of the forward list structure throughout these operations while adhering to the performance constraint. Although it doesn't document the design choices explicitly, you can easily understand the rationale behind them by reading the comments in the code.']

