The function create_pdu_list() generates unique RXI tags, RNTIs, and CRC_INDICATION_REL8_TAGs for each PDU, and employs a semaphore to synchronize logging to avoid data races or deadlocks. Performance monitoring is not explicitly implemented in this example but can be easily added by integrating a performance monitoring framework such as Google Perftools or SystemTap.

Memory usage and allocation overhead are minimized by using malloc_usable_size() to check the memory footprint of allocated blocks, although no explicit optimization for large volumes of data is included in this example. The trade-off between memory usage and access speed can be adjusted by modifying the concurrent container's internal buffer size or changing the underlying algorithms used by tbb::concurrent_vector.']

