- For thread safety, each deserialization operation is isolated within a try-finally block that ensures proper closing of the input stream and releases associated resources.
- However, the current implementation may not be suitable for high-concurrency environments as it does not offer any concurrent access control or synchronization mechanisms. Depending on your requirements, you may consider implementing locks, semaphores, or other concurrency control methods to ensure safe parallel access to shared resources.']

